# Obsidian Vault Content Conventions

## Frontmatter

- YAML block delimited by `---`
- Only include properties that will be queried -- no blank or placeholder values
- Use Templater `<% %>` syntax for dynamic prompts in templates

## Relationship Fields

Use wikilinks, not plain text slugs. This creates backlinks:

```yaml
customer: "[[Acme Corp]]"     # Good -- creates backlink
customer: acme-corp            # Bad -- no backlink, fragile
```

## Aliases

YAML list format only:

```yaml
aliases:
  - Acme
  - ACME Corp
```

## File Naming

- Evergreen notes: Title Case with spaces (`Acme Corp.md`)
- Dated notes: `YYYY-MM-DD - Title.md`

## Tags

Cross-cutting themes only: `#security`, `#observability`, `#search`, `#migration`. Never duplicate frontmatter. Flat namespace -- no nesting.

## Dataview Queries

- Always scope to folder: `FROM "03-Meetings"`
- Use DQL, not JavaScript queries
- Add `LIMIT` on list queries
- Use `SORT` for deterministic order

## Links

Wikilinks `[[Note Title]]` for all internal references. Shortest path format.

## Headings

- Every template starts with `# <% tp.file.title %>` for reading mode
- Body sections use H2 and below
- No skipped heading levels (H2 -> H3, never H2 -> H4)

## One Note, One Purpose

Each template produces one atomic note. Never combine multiple meetings or topics.
